    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **263 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `contactPreference` on the owner response so it returns `'EMAIL'` when an email is present, otherwise `'PHONE'`.\n\nThe `OwnerDto` is generated at build time from the OpenAPI spec and populated by a MapStruct mapper, so the change touched two files:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and it's documented in the API contract).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression that derives the value from the owner:\n   ```java\n   owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\"\n   ```\n\nThis flows through both `GET /api/owners/{id}` and the create response since both use `toOwnerDto`. The two new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) pass, and all 263 tests remain green.",
